    "PublishValidatedDraft": {
      "additionalProperties": false,
      "description": "Publish one gated wiring document into a named package version.\n\n# What this carries, and why each field is here (wamn-0h0g.7.10)\n\n`catalog.wirings` needs seven values. `tenant_id` is the authenticated scope's, `wiring_id` and `version` ride the document, and `graph_json` IS the document — but `package_id` and `package_version` ride NEITHER the document nor its hash, which is why `ctl author-wiring` takes both as separate argv. So the command carries them too, and the row is writable from this input alone.\n\n`wiring_hash` is DERIVED SERVER-SIDE and is deliberately absent here. The wamn-0h0g.7.8 close ruling rejected a carried proof value as forgeable and replayable and made the verb compute the identity from the bytes; a literal wire hash field the server trusted would reopen it. A client that wants to state its expectation states it out of band, not as the value written.\n\n`successful_report_id` is GONE. wamn-0h0g.8.5.6 collapsed the report id into `wiring_hash`, and the green-report guard reads the report BY that hash — so the field named an identity the document already determines and had no remaining reader.\n\nThe document rides as its own JSON rather than a typed carrier: these are the exact bytes `catalog.wirings.graph_json` stores, and [`wamn_catalog::WiringDocument::parse`] is the ONE validating reader for them. Typing the field here would put a second structural dialect in front of that one, and — measured — would need `schemars::JsonSchema` derives across `wamn-catalog` and the FROZEN `wamn-event-wire`, which `WiringEventOperation` aliases into. The server parses, validates and hashes; this is the carrier.",
      "properties": {
        "document": {
          "description": "The wiring document itself — `catalog.wirings.graph_json`."
        },
        "package-id": {
          "description": "Package identity the wiring is published into.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "package-version": {
          "description": "Exact package version whose component facts gate this document.",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "provenance": {
          "anyOf": [
            {
              "$ref": "#/definitions/CommitProvenance"
            },
            {
              "type": "null"
            }
          ],
          "description": "Optional source attribution written only to the authenticated command audit."
        },
        "scope": {
          "$ref": "#/definitions/AuthoringScope"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "document",
        "package-id",
        "package-version",
        "scope"
      ],
      "type": "object"
    },
